Warn when the session cookie exceeds the size a browser keeps

HorizonMiddleware._process_request in horizon/middleware/base.py checks
the size of a signed-cookie session on the request side: it sums the
cookies a request sends and logs "Total Cookie size ..." at ERROR once
they reach SESSION_COOKIE_MAX_SIZE (4093 bytes, horizon/defaults.py).
A browser discards a cookie of that size, so the request after the
login carries no session cookie and the check never runs. The login
answers with a redirect, the browser is on the login page again, the
page shows no reason, and Horizon logs nothing (#1845). With 71
services in the Keystone catalog, the login set a sessionid cookie of
4903 to 4919 bytes.

The patch adds SessionCookieSizeMiddleware in
horizon/middleware/session_cookie_size.py and lists it in
openstack_dashboard/settings.py directly before Django's
SessionMiddleware. SessionMiddleware sets the session cookie when the
response passes through it. HorizonMiddleware sits further in, so it
has returned before the cookie exists; a middleware listed before
SessionMiddleware sees the cookie as the browser does. When the
signed-cookie store is in use and the name plus the value of the
session cookie a response sets reach SESSION_COOKIE_MAX_SIZE, the
middleware logs "Session cookie for user_id: <id> is <n>B >= <max>B.
..." at ERROR and calls add_logout_reason with status "error". The
login page then shows "Your session is too large for a browser cookie
and the login cannot complete. Contact your administrator." in its
alert-danger box. SESSION_COOKIE_MAX_SIZE = None disables the check,
and every other session engine skips it.

The patch reports and does not refuse. The response is otherwise
unchanged, and a client that keeps a cookie of any size stays logged in
and only causes the log line. The patch adds no setting and needs no
operator configuration.

Tests: no upstream test lists openstack_dashboard.settings.MIDDLEWARE,
and the test settings of horizon, openstack_auth and openstack_dashboard
do not load the new entry, so no upstream test moves. The patch adds
the 12 tests of SessionCookieSizeMiddlewareTests in
horizon/test/unit/middleware/test_session_cookie_size.py. Ten call the
middleware with a stub response: a cookie over, at and under the limit,
another session engine, the setting at None, no and a deleted session
cookie, a custom SESSION_COOKIE_NAME, a request without a session, and
an exception from the inner chain. Two run it around Django's
SessionMiddleware: a large session is flagged and a small one is not,
and a large session of an HTTP 500 response sets no session cookie and
is not flagged.

Proof: test_session_cookie_size_is_announced in
tests/container-images/verify_horizon.sh asserts the MIDDLEWARE position
in the built image, sends a small and a large signed-cookie session
through the image's middleware chain and asserts the ERROR record and
the two cookies for the large one only, then follows the redirects from
LOGIN_REDIRECT_URL without the session cookie, as a browser does after
the login, and asserts that they end on the login page with the message
in its alert-danger box.

The 2026.1 twin carries the same hunks: horizon/middleware/__init__.py
and openstack_dashboard/settings.py are identical in 25.7.0 and 27.0.0,
and the other two files are new.

Applies to horizon 27.0.0 (2026.2).

Upstream status: not yet proposed.

